From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dtl: compile the ETW event sites out

traceloggingprovider.h is a Windows SDK header MinGW-w64 does not ship, and
it was the recorded compiler boundary. Route the tree at
compat/relay_tracelogging.hpp instead, which supplies TraceLoggingHProvider
as a distinct incomplete-type pointer and turns TraceLoggingWrite and
TraceLoggingProviderEnabled into a void expression and a false constant.

This changes no behaviour. Every TraceLoggingWrite in the pinned tree is
already guarded by `if (g_hTracelogging)`, the tree never calls
TRACELOGGING_DEFINE_PROVIDER or TraceLoggingRegister, and upstream's README
states that in the default configuration no provider is created and no data
is sent. This port never calls SetTraceloggingProvider, so the events were
inert at run time before this patch and are inert at compile time after it.

Error paths are untouched, which is what the port-quality roadmap requires of
this step. The events are measurement counters, and where one sits beside a
failure it is beside the error path rather than on it: PipelineState.cpp logs
inside `if (FAILED(hr))` and then calls ThrowFailure(hr) either way.

The ~71 guarded call sites are deliberately left in place. They cost nothing
once the macros are inert, and deleting them would be a large diff across
eight files that makes a later rebase onto a newer upstream materially harder.
external/MicrosoftTelemetry.h needs no change either: it is already a
vendored no-telemetry stub of macro constants, portable as it stands.

The compatibility macros do not name their parameters, so arguments are never
expanded and never evaluated. That is what lets the field macros in the call
sites stay undefined, and it is pinned by tests/relay_tracelogging_test.cpp
along with the void-expression and always-false properties.
---
diff --git a/include/D3D12TranslationLayerDependencyIncludes.h b/include/D3D12TranslationLayerDependencyIncludes.h
index 377d66e..aaacedb 100644
--- a/include/D3D12TranslationLayerDependencyIncludes.h
+++ b/include/D3D12TranslationLayerDependencyIncludes.h
@@ -70,7 +70,13 @@ using std::max;
 #endif
 
 #include <evntrace.h>
-#include <traceloggingprovider.h>
+// traceloggingprovider.h is a Windows SDK header MinGW-w64 does not ship,
+// and it was the recorded compiler boundary. The events behind it are
+// already inert in this port: every TraceLoggingWrite below is guarded by
+// `if (g_hTracelogging)`, this tree never registers a provider, and nothing
+// calls SetTraceloggingProvider. The replacement compiles the event sites
+// to nothing while leaving every HRESULT path untouched.
+#include "relay_tracelogging.hpp"
 #include <MicrosoftTelemetry.h>
 
 #define INITGUID
